WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.549
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:14.369
Unit nineteen: At the Hotel. In this unit, you will make polite requests at a hotel.

4
00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:16.350
Hotel.

5
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.723
Hotel means a building where you pay to stay the night.

6
00:00:20.023 --> 00:00:21.720
Our hotel is near the beach.

7
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.212
Your turn. Say: Hotel.

8
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:28.878
Hotel.

9
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:30.792
Reception.

10
00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:34.304
Reception means the desk at the entrance of a hotel.

11
00:00:34.604 --> 00:00:36.069
Please ask at reception.

12
00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.700
Your turn. Say: Reception.

13
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.413
Reception.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.035
Room.

15
00:00:45.735 --> 00:00:48.651
Room means a space in a building with walls and a door.

16
00:00:48.951 --> 00:00:50.521
Our room has two beds.

17
00:00:51.221 --> 00:00:53.479
Your turn. Say: Room.

18
00:00:56.179 --> 00:00:56.785
Room.

19
00:00:57.783 --> 00:00:58.425
Key.

20
00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.263
Key means a thing that opens a door.

21
00:01:01.563 --> 00:01:02.866
Here is your room key.

22
00:01:03.566 --> 00:01:05.441
Your turn. Say: Key.

23
00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:08.817
Key.

24
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:10.980
Reservation.

25
00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.027
Reservation means an arrangement to keep a room or table for you.

26
00:01:15.327 --> 00:01:17.593
We have a reservation for two nights.

27
00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:20.934
Your turn. Say: Reservation.

28
00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:24.647
Reservation.

29
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.581
Check in.

30
00:01:27.281 --> 00:01:29.966
Check in means to arrive at a hotel and get your room.

31
00:01:30.266 --> 00:01:31.917
We checked in at two o'clock.

32
00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:34.898
Your turn. Say: Check in.

33
00:01:37.598 --> 00:01:38.448
Check in.

34
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.358
Check out.

35
00:01:41.058 --> 00:01:43.151
Check out means to pay and leave a hotel.

36
00:01:43.451 --> 00:01:44.800
We check out at noon.

37
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.350
Your turn. Say: Check out.

38
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:51.981
Check out.

39
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:53.892
Breakfast.

40
00:01:54.592 --> 00:01:56.905
Breakfast means the first meal of the day.

41
00:01:57.205 --> 00:01:59.088
Breakfast is from seven to ten.

42
00:01:59.788 --> 00:02:02.522
Your turn. Say: Breakfast.

43
00:02:05.222 --> 00:02:06.292
Breakfast.

44
00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:09.364
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.664 --> 00:02:12.409
Good afternoon. Could we check in, please?

46
00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:16.183
Of course. Do you have a reservation?

47
00:02:17.483 --> 00:02:20.275
Yes, for a family room. The name is Chan.

48
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:24.596
Here's your key. Room 305.

49
00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:28.629
Thank you. Could I ask what time breakfast is?

50
00:02:29.917 --> 00:02:32.941
Breakfast is at seven. Enjoy your stay!

51
00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.239
Grammar focus: Polite requests (Could I ?).

52
00:02:37.539 --> 00:02:40.540
Could I have the key, please? Could we check in?

53
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.546
'Could I ...?' is more polite than 'Can I ...?' Always add 'please'.

54
00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:48.400
Now read and listen. A Night at the Hotel.

55
00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.558
When we arrived at the hotel, we went to reception.

56
00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.723
My dad said, “Could we check in, please?”

57
00:02:57.017 --> 00:02:59.214
We had a reservation for a family room.

58
00:03:00.517 --> 00:03:03.689
The receptionist gave us a key and said breakfast was at seven.

59
00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:06.855
The next day, we checked out at noon.

60
00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.768
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:11.068 --> 00:03:12.846
blank I have the key, please?

62
00:03:13.146 --> 00:03:16.115
A, Could. B, Do. C, Am.

63
00:03:20.117 --> 00:03:21.954
The answer is A: Could.

64
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.868
The desk at the entrance of a hotel is blank.

65
00:03:26.168 --> 00:03:30.007
A, reception. B, breakfast. C, room.

66
00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:36.411
The answer is A: reception.

67
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.812
To pay and leave a hotel is to blank.

68
00:03:40.112 --> 00:03:44.067
A, check out. B, check in. C, reserve.

69
00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:50.280
The answer is A: check out.

70
00:03:51.783 --> 00:03:55.446
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you say when you check in at a hotel?

71
00:04:00.746 --> 00:04:05.841
I say, “Good afternoon. We have a reservation. Could we check in, please?”

72
00:04:06.141 --> 00:04:07.967
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:08.983 --> 00:04:13.403
Great work today! You learned eight new words and polite requests (could i ?).

74
00:04:13.703 --> 00:04:17.238
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

75
00:04:17.538 --> 00:04:20.120
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

76
00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:23.003
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

